To create a pivot table in Excel, select your data range (ensure it has headers), go to the Insert tab, click PivotTable, choose "New Worksheet," and click OK. Then, drag fields from the panel into Rows, Columns, or Values areas to analyze your data.  


Step-by-Step Instructions: 

Prepare Data: Ensure your data is in a clean, tabular format with headers in the top row and no empty rows or columns. 

Insert PivotTable: Click any cell inside your data range. 

Launch Tool: Navigate to the Insert tab and click PivotTable. 

Select Range & Location: The "Create PivotTable" dialog box will appear. It should automatically select your data range. Select New Worksheet to place the table elsewhere, then click OK. 

Build the Report: In the "PivotTable Fields" pane on the right, drag and drop fields into the four areas: 

Rows: Items you want to group (e.g., Salesperson, Product). 

Values: Numerical data to calculate (e.g., Revenue, Quantity). 

Columns: Categories to compare across (e.g., Month, Region). 

Filters: Fields to restrict the data shown.  

